<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
    <parent>
        <groupId>org.eclipse.deeplearning4j</groupId>
        <artifactId>kompile-app-parent</artifactId>
        <version>0.1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>kompile-app-web-shared</artifactId>
    <name>Kompile App - Shared Web Layer</name>
    <description>
        The web layer every persona app mounts: project browsing and portability, fact sheets,
        documents, sources and source providers, the index browser, knowledge and sync endpoints,
        k-app config, setup status, read-only model status, and the SPA forward controller.

        Also carries GlobalExceptionHandler. Nothing references it — it is discovered by component
        scan — so the reference closure misses it, but the @ControllerAdvice bean is only registered
        by the module that ships it. Left behind in kompile-app-main, the chat and crawl apps would
        boot with no advice and return opaque 500s instead of {error, message, type}.

        Per docs/architecture/app-persona-boundary.md this module is mounted by all three apps, so
        types it owns are automatically available to web-chat, web-crawl, web-graph and web-admin.
        That is what resolves the eight admin+shared support types (the staging-client cluster,
        ProjectBackendService, ProjectGraphPortabilityService, ProjectResponse,
        EmbeddingStatusBroadcaster) without duplicating them.

        Packages are preserved (ai.kompile.app.web.controllers, ai.kompile.app.project,
        ai.kompile.app.projectstore, ai.kompile.app.staging.*, ai.kompile.app.scaffold,
        ai.kompile.app.services, ai.kompile.app.subprocess.model) — the move is git mv plus pom
        wiring, so native-image reflect/resource config and every existing import are unaffected.
        Isolation comes from classpath presence, not package naming.

        Verified zero back-edges into kompile-app-main.
    </description>

    <dependencies>
